<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Emile Griffith returns with his care partner. He finished twelve sessions of cognitive processing therapy five weeks ago. He says he no longer blames himself in the same way: he went into the ring to win, not to hurt anyone, and he can now speak about his opponent without dreading the memory. Nightmares come about once a week. He takes sertraline 50 mg each morning without nausea, dizziness or bleeding. He completed ten sessions of physical therapy two weeks ago and does the home exercises most days; he has had no falls. His care partner notices no change in his memory. No thoughts of suicide. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>PCL-5</td><td>26, from 41 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>5; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Sodium</td><td>137 mmol/L on sertraline 50 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Nightmares</td><td>About once a week</td></tr><tr><td>Timed Up and Go</td><td>10 seconds</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

