    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-traumatic stress disorder, chronic (F43.12)</content>. Clinically meaningful response: PCL-5 26 from 41 (a fall of 15 points) after a full course of cognitive processing therapy and sertraline 50 mg. Sodium normal. No thoughts of suicide. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg.</item><item>Booster therapy sessions on request.</item><item>Safety plan and 988 reviewed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Mild cognitive impairment (G31.84)</content>. Stable by history; strategies working; balance better after physical therapy. [S]<list><item>Continue the home exercise program and daily walks.</item><item>MoCA at the yearly review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive testing (MoCA)</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly, or sooner with change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 22 at intake; no change reported; next at the yearly review</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Staging (CDR) and function (ADL and IADL)</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>CDR 0.5 at two weeks; function unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Medicine review for anticholinergic, sedating and fall-risk drugs (Beers)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg only</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Neuropsychiatric symptom screen (apathy, irritability, paranoia, impulsivity)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No apathy, irritability, paranoia or impulsive behavior</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 with suicide-risk review (item 9 and structured questions)</td><td>Monthly during acute treatment; every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 5, item 9 scored 0; no thoughts of suicide</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PCL-5</td><td>Baseline, then at each chronic-care visit during treatment; response judged after 8 to 12 weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCL-5 26: a clinically meaningful 15-point fall</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Sertraline: nausea, sleep, falls, bleeding, and sodium (SSRIs can lower sodium in older adults)</td><td>Two weeks after starting and after each dose change; sodium at those points</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Deviation: the sodium check ordered for two to four weeks after the increase to 50 mg was not done, because no visit fell then and the lab-only appointment was never scheduled. It was done today, three months after the increase: 137 mmol/L, normal, with no confusion, falls or other sign of low sodium, so no harm is known. Corrective action: a lab-only appointment is now booked automatically with any antidepressant start or dose change</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Trauma-focused psychotherapy (cognitive processing therapy)</td><td>Weekly, about twelve sessions</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Twelve sessions completed five weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall risk (Timed Up and Go, gait and balance), STEADI</td><td>At diagnosis, yearly, and after any fall</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 10 seconds; no falls</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Physical therapy for balance and strength</td><td>Once, after a Timed Up and Go above 12 seconds</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Ten sessions completed two weeks ago; home program continues</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Travel, money and home safety</td><td>At diagnosis and each follow-up</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No episodes of getting lost; shared oversight of bills working</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Care partner support and burden (Zarit Burden Interview, narrative)</td><td>At diagnosis, then every 6 to 12 months</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Zarit 14 at the diagnosis visit; his care partner attends the caregiver class; next check at about six months</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning</td><td>At diagnosis; revisit yearly and at changes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Health care agent named and goals recorded at the annual wellness visit six weeks ago; reviewed today without change</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Vascular risk factors (blood pressure, weight)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Blood pressure 128/76 mmHg; weight 73.9 kg</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Find the cause of the memory problems and explain it to him in a way he can take in. Outcome by 2026-06-16: Mild cognitive impairment most likely due to traumatic brain injury; explained with his care partner present, at his request, with a written summary [S]</item><item>A clinically meaningful fall in PTSD symptoms (PCL-5 down at least 10 points) by four months. Outcome by 2026-09-15: PCL-5 from 41 to 26 after cognitive processing therapy and sertraline [S]</item><item>Nightmares no more than about once a week, with at least six hours of sleep most nights. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item><item>No falls, with a balance and strength program. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item><item>Name a health care agent and record his goals of care while he can take part fully. Outcome by 2026-08-04: Health care agent named and goals of care recorded at the annual wellness visit [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for specialty care (2024); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Depression/Bipolar/Mood Disorders monographs (2026); American Geriatrics Society 2023 updated AGS Beers Criteria for potentially inappropriate medication use in older adults (2023); STEADI (Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths and Injuries): Clinical Resources (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month review in six weeks with PCL-5 and PHQ-9, influenza vaccine and the second zoster dose. Call the clinic or 988 at any time if thoughts of suicide arise. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-27: six-month review: PTSD, mood, cognition, safety and the plan for the year ahead. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
